Enable a bounded HTTP disk cache independently of the cache model.

The ship config keeps ATLANTIC_CACHE_MODEL=viewer (CacheModel::DocumentViewer):
smallest in-RAM object caches, no back/forward cache - that is the footprint
lever that stopped the reddit hard-OOMs on the 3.5 GB device. But
DocumentViewer also hardwires calculateURLCacheDiskCapacity() to 0, so the
NetworkProcess runs with NO HTTP disk cache at all (device-verified:
~/.cache/org.atlantic is 8 KB after heavy use, while the stock Gecko browser
keeps a many-MB cache2). The cost lands exactly where the browser feels
slowest: every repeat visit re-downloads every subresource (JS bundles, fonts,
images) over the radio instead of reading flash, and nothing is ever served as
a cheap 304 revalidation.

WEBKIT_URL_CACHE_DISK_CAPACITY_MB=<n> makes calculateURLCacheDiskCapacity()
return n MB regardless of cache model, giving a BOUNDED on-flash cache (the
NetworkCache evicts to stay under capacity, and low disk space still shrinks
it via NetworkProcess) without re-inflating any RAM-side cache.
deploy/runtime-common.sh ships 100 MB. Unset or 0 = stock behaviour for the
model, so light configs and A/B runs are unaffected.

The capacity is computed in the NetworkProcess (NetworkProcess::setCacheModel),
which receives the env from the firejail profile env block (sandboxed) or the
launcher wrapper (unconfined). The sailjail profile must also whitelist
~/.cache/wpe - WebKit's default cache tree, where WebKitCache lives - or the
NetworkProcess writes vanish into the jail; done in build-rpms-native.sh
alongside this patch.

--- a/Source/WebKit/Shared/CacheModel.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/Shared/CacheModel.cpp
@@ -26,8 +26,9 @@
 #include "config.h"
 #include "CacheModel.h"
 
 #include <algorithm>
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <wtf/RAMSize.h>
 #include <wtf/Seconds.h>
 #include <wtf/StdLibExtras.h>
 
@@ -128,6 +129,18 @@
 uint64_t calculateURLCacheDiskCapacity(CacheModel cacheModel, uint64_t diskFreeSize)
 {
+    // Atlantic: WEBKIT_URL_CACHE_DISK_CAPACITY_MB overrides the cache-model-
+    // derived HTTP disk cache capacity. The ship cache model (DocumentViewer,
+    // the RAM/OOM lever on the 3.5 GB device) hardwires the DISK cache to 0,
+    // so every repeat visit re-downloads all subresources - a large share of
+    // perceived "slow page loading". A bounded on-flash cache restores
+    // repeat-visit speed without moving any RAM knob. Unset or 0 = stock
+    // capacity for the model. See webkit-url-cache-disk-capacity-env.patch.
+    if (const char* capacityMB = getenv("WEBKIT_URL_CACHE_DISK_CAPACITY_MB")) {
+        if (long mb = atol(capacityMB); mb > 0)
+            return static_cast<uint64_t>(mb) * MB;
+    }
+
     uint64_t urlCacheDiskCapacity;
 
     switch (cacheModel) {
